# HarfBuzz-NG for PDFium

Name: HarfBuzz
URL: https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz
Version: See harfbuzz_revision in DEPS
Revision: See harfbuzz_revision in DEPS
License: MIT

## Purpose
HarfBuzz is used in PDFium for:
1. Font subsetting during document sanitization (removing unused glyphs)
2. Creating minimal font subsets when embedding new text (free text annotations)

## Subsetting API
We only use the hb-subset.h API which provides:
- hb_subset_input_create_or_fail()
- hb_subset_input_glyph_set()
- hb_subset_or_fail()

## Build Configuration
The library is built with subsetting support enabled. We do not use HarfBuzz's
shaping functionality (which would require additional dependencies).

## Local Modifications
None - we use the upstream source directly.
